What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/*/call_events
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        Enceka <enceka@yeah.net>
Description:
                Read-only call-event snapshot from both SIPC URC channels and
                the command reply channel. Each line contains:

                <sequence> <channel hint> <RING|STATE|END|DIAL>

                The latest 64 events are retained. poll(POLLPRI) wakes on a
                new event; reading does not consume entries. No caller number
                or raw payload is exposed. Sequence starts at one per load.

                A channel hint (0 or 1) is not a reliable source SIM: firmware
                may route either SIM onto one channel. Consumers must query
                both cards' CLCC through the AT owner, retaining that query's
                source card on each call. Events only request a refresh; they
                never start, accept, or end a call.
